1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,176
I rented a berth for a boat we didn't
own. By closing, someone else paid

2
00:00:06,176 --> 00:00:07,000
our debt.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,353
Our buyer kept payment in a waterproof
tube beneath the pier. The gate

4
00:00:12,353 --> 00:00:14,000
required a mooring receipt.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,706
Jason suggested swimming. I suggested
paperwork, because the notice

6
00:00:17,706 --> 00:00:21,000
promised a refund if our berth was
occupied.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,600
We paid at the machine. Then I
photographed the buyer's skiff, blocking

8
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:28,000
our rented berth.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:33,353
The receipt opened the gate. Jason
collected the tube while I requested a

10
00:00:33,353 --> 00:00:35,000
refund at the kiosk.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,200
The kiosk charged the blocking boat's
deposit and returned our rental. Our

12
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:42,000
buyer had left his registration on the
bow.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,941
Inside the tube, our fee was complete.
Jason asked whether taking the

14
00:00:46,941 --> 00:00:49,000
skiff would complicate my arrangement.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,900
I said it would. Then I untied it
anyway, and let him explain the

16
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:56,000
paperwork while we left Vice City.
